  "term": "reality therapy",
  "definition": "Reality therapy is a form of psychotherapy that emphasizes a person’s responsibility for their own behavior. In this approach, the therapist takes an active role in helping the person see themselves more accurately so they can meet needs for self-worth while respecting others.",
